/*!
    \page creator-how-to-run-on-harmonyos.html
    \previouspage creator-how-tos.html

    \ingroup creator-how-to-harmonyos
    \ingroup creator-how-to-run

    \title Run on HarmonyOS devices

    To build an application and run it on a device:

    \list 1
        \li Connect the device, as described in
            \l {Connect HarmonyOS devices}.
        \li Set the HarmonyOS SDK location and the signing material in
            \preferences > \uicontrol SDKs > \uicontrol HarmonyOS, as described
            in \l {Set up the HarmonyOS SDK} and
            \l {Sign HarmonyOS packages}.
        \li Activate the kit that has the device as its run device.
        \li Select \imagerunsmall (\uicontrol Run).
    \endlist

    Running deploys first, and the whole chain is
    \c harmonydeployqt, \c hvigor, \c hap-sign-tool, \c {hdc install}, and
    \c {aa start}. The run then stays alive as long as the application does, by
    following its \c hilog output. Stopping it force-stops the application.

    \section1 Debug on a device

    Select \uicontrol Debug > \uicontrol {Start Debugging} >
    \uicontrol {Start Debugging of Startup Project}. The application starts, a
    debug server starts inside it, \QC attaches to that, and breakpoints
    resolve both in the application and in Qt.

    Choose where to put a breakpoint with the attach in mind. The device
    refuses \c PTRACE_TRACEME, so nothing can be launched under the debugger
    and \QC attaches to an application that is already running. Whatever
    \c main() reaches directly has therefore happened before the debugger
    gets there. Put the breakpoint somewhere the event loop reaches later,
    such as a slot or a destructor.

    Frames in the system libraries stay nameless. Symbols are matched against
    local copies of what the process mapped, and there are none for the
    HarmonyOS framework.

    \section1 Troubleshoot errors

    \section2 A debug run fails without a message

    A \QC that did not shut down cleanly leaves an \c hdc port forwarding
    behind, and \c hdc refuses a second forwarding to the same remote port.
    List ports with \c {hdc fport ls} and remove the stale one with
    \c {hdc fport rm <local> <remote>}.

    \section2 The application starts and quits at once

    The application found no libraries to load. Check that
    \uicontrol {Additional packages} points at the prefix the third-party
    libraries are installed under, as described in
    \l {Specify HarmonyOS deploy settings}. The device reports this as an
    ArkTS \c TypeError that names nothing useful.

    \section2 The application ignores a changed argument

    \c {aa start} passes its parameters as arguments only when the process
    starts, so an application that is still running keeps the old ones. Stop it
    first.

    \section2 Packaging fails, or the package is gone

    Use command-line tools 6.1 or newer. Version 6.0.2 deletes the generated
    project directly after packaging, and takes the package with it.

    \section2 The build fails with "cmake: not found"

    The build directory outlived the Qt it was configured with. Reset the CMake
    configuration for the kit.

    \section1 What is not possible

    \list
        \li Stopping in code that runs before the debugger attaches, such as a
            static initializer or the early part of \c main().
        \li Debugging an application that is not a Qt one. The debug server is
            shipped and started as part of the Qt application package, and
            there is no other foothold.
    \endlist

    \sa {HarmonyOS}{How to: Develop for HarmonyOS},
    {Developing for HarmonyOS devices},
    {Manage kits}{How to: Manage kits}, {Managing kits},
    {Running applications}, {Specify HarmonyOS deploy settings}
*/
